  "question": {
    "text": "Incandescent bulbs are designed by keeping in mind that the resistance of their filament increases with the increase in temperature. If at room temperature, $100 \\mathrm{~W}, 60 \\mathrm{~W}$ and $40 \\mathrm{~W}$ bulbs have filament resistances $R_{100}, R_{60}$ and $R_{40}$, respectively, the relation between these resistances is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "zVZ9Y",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{R_{100}}=\\frac{1}{R_{40}}+\\frac{1}{R_{60}}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "9zohO",
      "text": "\n$R_{100}=R_{40}+R_{60}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "dyYNl",
      "text": "\n$R_{100}>R_{60}>R_{40}$\n",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "Kw51L",
      "text": "\n$\\frac{1}{R_{100}}>\\frac{1}{R_{60}}>\\frac{1}{R_{40}}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$R=\\frac{V^2}{P}$ or $R \\propto \\frac{1}{P}$ $\\therefore \\quad \\frac{1}{R_{100}}>\\frac{1}{R_{60}}>\\frac{1}{R_{40}}$\nHence, the correct option is (d).",
    "image": null
  },
